    "rationale": "Fix over rounds 1-2: the second B tile offset is now 1280 + 16*i, i.e. 16*80 + 16*i, the true start of B rows 16..31 in the 32x80 row-major layout. The prior offset 80 + 16*i loaded B rows 1..16, so cell products paired A[k=16..31] with the wrong B rows, causing the product-sequence mismatch at every cell (written but wrong operands). Structure: A's two 16x16 tiles (offsets 0 and 16, slot-0 stride 32) are loaded once into spad rows 0 and 16 and reused across all 5 column blocks \u2014 minimal A traffic of 512 bytes. Per block i = 0..N//16-1: mvin B(k=0..15) tile at offset 16*i into spad 32 (slot-1 stride 80), preload with overwrite out_addr 2684354560 (bit31|bit29, acc row 0), compute A tile 0 with accumulated=false and bd=4294967295; mvin B(k=16..31) tile at offset 1280 + 16*i into spad 48, preload with accumulate out_addr 3758096384 (bit31|bit30|bit29), compute A tile at spad 16 with accumulated=false; then mvout acc rows 0..15 (acc_addr 2684354560) to C element offset 16*i with store stride 320 (80 int32). Reduction order is k=0..15 then k=16..31, increasing K-index per cell, and K*16384 = 524288 <= 2147483647. Total mvin bytes: 2*256 (A) + 10*256 (B) = 3072, minimal since A is 16x32 = 512 int8 bytes and B is 32x80 = 2560 int8 bytes with every element used and each tile loaded exactly once. Scratchpad usage: tiles at rows 0, 16, 32, 48 (48+16 = 64 <= 80), all 16-aligned; accumulator rows 0..15 within 16. Expanded commands: 6 setup + 7*5 loop + 1 fence = 42, minimal given 12 mandatory mvins, 10 computes each requiring a preload, 5 mvouts, 4 configs, and a final fence."
